Goose is an extensible open-source AI agent built in Rust that automates
complex software engineering tasks from the command line. It plans, writes,
edits, builds, and tests code autonomously across OpenAI, Anthropic, Google,
Ollama, llama.cpp, and any OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint.

This OpenBSD port is built 100% JIT-free for strict W^X environments, pairing
Model Context Protocol (MCP) server/extension orchestration, SQLite session
persistence, and tree-sitter code analysis with a pure-Rust boa_engine
JavaScript interpreter for token-efficient code-mode tool execution.
